    {
      "source_record": "data/ingredients/mapped/Carnitine_Hydrochloride.yaml",
      "shape": "synonym_retirement",
      "before_yaml_sha256": "c123a3f76cf2277ca68a08c99e58f96845842fd90c75bdd19b90ab8db7bb6780",
      "after_yaml_sha256": "c03c1c66b9e70436da2e841d1edf2a700f05830674c715fc265ac7fde9705722",
      "change": "Retyped '4-amino-2-hydroxy-N,N,N-trimethyl-4-oxobutan-1-aminium chloride' from EXACT_SYNONYM to REJECTED_LABEL, preserving its original chebi_synonym_review source (#1003; #669). Official ChEBI:48601 assigns this exact IUPAC name to carnitinamide chloride (C7H17N2O2.Cl), whereas CHEBI:17126 carnitine is C7H15NO3. The amide name survived this record's 2026-07-05 correction of the erroneous CHEBI:48601 mapping. Sources inspected 2026-11-01: https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/api/ontologies/chebi/terms?obo_id=CHEBI:48601 ; https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/api/ontologies/chebi/terms?obo_id=CHEBI:17126 . Preserved the current identifier, parent mapping, status and occurrences; unresolved salt/CAS/stereochemistry questions are not adjudicated, and no scientific or release approval is asserted.",
      "verification": "Official ChEBI:48601 assigns this exact IUPAC name to carnitinamide chloride (C7H17N2O2.Cl), whereas CHEBI:17126 carnitine is C7H15NO3. The amide name survived this record's 2026-07-05 correction of the erroneous CHEBI:48601 mapping. Sources inspected 2026-11-01: https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/api/ontologies/chebi/terms?obo_id=CHEBI:48601 ; https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/api/ontologies/chebi/terms?obo_id=CHEBI:17126 . The historical DL-carnitine parent-row alias is deliberately retained pending the unresolved exact salt/stereochemistry decision (#669). Its omission by the raw generator is not scientific evidence for removal. Generated source provenance is not fresh identity support for this retained token; original provenance remains in the receipt before-row and the archived baseline."
    },
